# Postgres connection string — use a French-hosted instance (Scaleway/OVHcloud)
# even for local dev if you want to test the data-residency story end to end.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/conforma?schema=public"

# Auth (NextAuth) — placeholder until the real provider (Keycloak, per spec §3) is wired in
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="replace-with-a-random-32-byte-string"

# One Google Cloud OAuth client (Web application) powers TWO unrelated
# features, so it needs BOTH of these redirect URIs registered on it:
#   {origin}/api/auth/callback/google        -> mailbox connection (spec §5.11)
#   {origin}/api/auth/callback/google-login  -> "Continuer avec Google" on /login
# The second one is deliberately not the default "google" id — that path is
# already taken by the mailbox callback (see src/lib/auth.ts).
# Setting these also makes the Google button appear on /login; leave them
# empty and it stays hidden entirely. Google sign-in only authenticates
# already-created, active, non-learner accounts — it never creates one.
# See README for the full walkthrough.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=""
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Encrypts MailboxConnection's stored OAuth tokens at rest (AES-256-GCM) —
# 32 random bytes, base64. Generate with:
# node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# AI — platform-level, not per-organization (see src/lib/ai.ts): one key,
# billed to Conforma, powers "Assister avec l'IA" and "Extraire avec l'IA"
# for every tenant. Get one at platform.openai.com (API keys, separate from
# a personal ChatGPT Plus subscription — needs its own billing set up).
OPENAI_API_KEY=""

# Transactional email — platform-level too (see src/lib/brevo.ts): one
# Brevo account sends for every tenant (Team invites, convocations,
# positioning test, contract, platform access). BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL must be
# a domain verified in your Brevo account (Senders & IP > Domains) — the
# recipient still sees the organization's own name as the sender name.
BREVO_API_KEY=""
BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL=""

# Where "demander une intégration" requests are emailed (see
# /api/integrations/requests). Optional: falls back to BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL,
# which is by definition a mailbox you control, so a deployment that can
# send email can always receive these. The request is stored in
# IntegrationRequest either way — the email is the notification, not the
# record.
PLATFORM_CONTACT_EMAIL=""

# LMS file storage — platform-level (see src/lib/storage.ts): one Vercel
# Blob store holds every tenant's uploaded module videos/documents, same
# "Conforma owns the infra, tenants just use the feature" pattern as
# OPENAI_API_KEY/BREVO_API_KEY above. Create a Blob store in the Vercel
# dashboard (Storage tab) and either run `vercel env pull` or copy the
# token it gives you — works identically in local dev and production
# (unlike writing to local disk, which breaks on Vercel's serverless
# filesystem).
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# E-signature — Jalon's own Yousign/Youtrust PARTNER account (ISV pricing
# negotiated July 2026). Fallback only: an org's own key on /integrations
# always wins and bypasses metering entirely. Signatures running on this
# platform key are counted per org by src/lib/signatureQuota.ts (Solo plan:
# 10/month included, 1 € HT re-billed beyond). YOUSIGN_WEBHOOK_SECRET is
# the signing secret of the single webhook subscription created in Jalon's
# own Youtrust app, pointing at {origin}/api/webhooks/yousign/platform.
# Leave both empty until the partner contract is signed — orgs with their
# own key keep working, everyone else gets the free internal stub.
YOUSIGN_API_KEY=""
YOUSIGN_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# E-invoicing connector (spec §5.3 / §7.2) — client chooses their own provider,
# so these are per-tenant credentials in the real app, not global env vars.
# Left here only as a placeholder for local testing against one sandbox account.
PENNYLANE_API_KEY=""

# Bank reconciliation, tier 2 (see src/lib/bridge.ts) — Bridge
# (bridgeapi.io), a French DSP2/ACPR-licensed open-banking aggregator
# covering ~99% of French banks + ~200 more across the EU through one API.
# Platform-level (like OPENAI_API_KEY/BREVO_API_KEY above): Jalon's own
# developer account brokers each org's own bank consent, Jalon never holds
# banking credentials or touches the money itself. Unlike some aggregators,
# Bridge has no self-serve free production tier — the sandbox (free,
# self-service at https://dashboard.bridgeapi.io/signup) is enough to build
# and test against, but going live needs a commercial agreement with
# Bridge. Leave empty to hide "Connecter ma banque" entirely — tier 1 (CSV
# import, always on) doesn't need this.
#
# (An earlier version of this integration targeted GoCardless Bank Account
# Data instead — dropped because GoCardless closed new signups for that
# product before this app ever went live with it.)
BRIDGE_CLIENT_ID=""
BRIDGE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Shared by both cron jobs (see vercel.json) — Vercel sends this
# automatically as `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` once the env var
# exists; until then the cron routes run unauthenticated (fine for local
# dev, not for production). Generate with:
# node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
CRON_SECRET=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mesure marketing (côté client) — voir src/components/CookieConsent.tsx.
# Ces variables DOIVENT être préfixées NEXT_PUBLIC_ pour être exposées au
# navigateur. Tant qu'elles sont vides, AUCUNE balise n'est chargée et la
# bannière de consentement ne s'affiche pas (no-op complet).
# Le chargement des balises est conditionné au consentement RGPD de l'utilisateur.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID              — Google Analytics 4 (format "G-XXXXXXXXXX")
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID             — Google Tag Manager (format "GTM-XXXXXXX"), alternative à GA4 direct
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID      — Meta/Facebook Pixel (identifiant numérique)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_LINKEDIN_PARTNER_ID — LinkedIn Insight Tag (Partner ID numérique)
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_LINKEDIN_PARTNER_ID=""

# "Réserver une démo" button on the public landing page (BookDemoButton) —
# opens this as a Calendly popup. Free Calendly account: create an event
# type (e.g. "Démo Jalon — 30 min"), copy its scheduling link
# (https://calendly.com/<you>/<event>) here. Must be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_
# to reach the browser. Leave empty to hide the button entirely.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CALENDLY_URL=""
